#: ../../reference/cli.rst:327
msgid "guidedog publish"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:330
msgid "Builds the project that a registered publisher's configuration names, as HTML with Guidedog's own engine, freezes the site, and has the publisher plan and publish it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:338
msgid "``--dry-run`` builds and plans, and writes nothing to the target. ``--wait=SECONDS`` is how long to wait for the host to confirm the deployment (``0``: do not wait). ``--timeout=SECONDS`` bounds each whole exchange with the publisher, including writing the request (default: 300 seconds). Choose a value longer than ``--wait``. A timeout or Ctrl+C after a possible write reports an unknown outcome: run the publisher's recovery command before retrying. ``--verbose`` lists every change. Each invocation builds into its own private folder, which is removed on release; concurrent invocations cannot change each other's snapshots. See :doc:`../plugins`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:347
msgid "guidedog plugin"
